AB  - Security Operations Centers (SOCs) face increasing operational pressure from growing alert volumes, diverse telemetry, and manual triage demands, while traditional SIEM and SOAR workflows—limited by static rules and sequential processing—struggle to scale. This paper presents an agentic, asynchronous alert-enrichment framework that reimagines enrichment as a parallel evidence-gathering and reasoning task performed by an autonomous agent integrating policy checks, multi-source asynchronous intelligence collection, LLM-based semantic analysis, and confidence-driven decision control with optional human escalation. A prototype built with modular connectors and an asynchronous execution model is evaluated under rising alert concurrency, demonstrating low overhead, stable latency, and reliable operation even under stress. Security analysis further highlights protections against adversarial inputs and unsafe automation. The results show that agentic AI can function as a practical, governance-aware accelerator for real-time SOC alert enrichment.
