AB  - As the Metaverse is rapidly evolving, the security framework of the system will need to evolve to protect users against more cyberattacks. The growing rise in the size of Large Language Models (LLMs) has amplified risks of email phishing attacks, ransomware hits, data breaches, and state-sponsored attacks that have become more advanced and require smarter and adaptive responses. To meet this requirement, different secure services are provided by the use of AI-based, web-based cybersecurity ecosystem, called SecureNet that combines threat-monitoring, anomaly-detection, geolocation of attack that allows tracking the attack origin, quantum inspired encryption, and deceptionbased defense mechanisms. It is based on cyberpunk-themed dashboards, the system is built on Python-Flask server code that uses dynamic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript elements to represent real-time cyber-attack conditions. The fundamental modules that incorporate the live scoring of threats, IP geolocation tracking, trap files identification, emergency lockdown measures, and MirrorNet-based simulation of threats that are effective to test the incorporation of modern cyber defense systems. It has an architecture based on a modular clientserver model that allows continuous updates, simulated API-based interaction of data and responsive UI interaction. System testing to validate the stable operation of all modules, visualizing threats, mapping of geolocation accurately, and simulated lockdown performance, and smooth running of quantum key distribution logic are all confirmed. Combining the tricks of deception and AI-powered analytics, as well as accessible and intuitive visualization, SecureNet offers a scalable and easy-to-learn environment to learn about cyber-attack behavior and defensive response flows. This project exemplifies the potential to design lightweight technologies into extensive, impactful, and real-time cybersecurity simulation that may be applied to develop academic learning, conduct prototyping, and, subsequently, expand to fully autonomous cyber defense infrastructures.
