AB  - Security Operations Centers (SOCs) process large volumes of alerts detected by SIEM platforms and handled through SOAR workflows. This paper presents a constrained agentic AI component integrated into a SIEM/SOAR environment to support incident triage. The system follows an end-toend workflow (SOAR → application server → SIEM enrichment → on-premise LLM-based reasoning → structured response → SOAR) and uses locally deployed open-source models under enterprise confidentiality constraints rather than a cloud-hosted conversational service. The implementation separates deterministic enrichment and execution from probabilistic reasoning and enforces structured fail-closed outputs. We also summarize the model adaptation path used during development: prompt-only instruction-tuned models, a hardware-constrained LoRA stage, and finally full fine-tuning of GPT-2, selected as the smallest practical baseline under the available on-premise hardware constraints.
