AB  - We describe the design of a capture-the-flag like testbed and use it to study the cognitive vulnerabilities of human penetration testers and compare them against those of an LLM-based agent. We find significant differences between the humans and the LLM for most cognitive vulnerabilities. We conclude that testing the cognitive vulnerabilities of LLMs in cyber security settings require different testbeds than for humans due to differences in how LLM-based agents perceive and process their environment, and these differences influence how defensive measures targeted at LLM-based should be implemented.
ER  - 

