AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) has become rapidly integral to modern warfare, transforming both cyber operations and conventional military tactics in 2024. This review surveys AI deployment in offensive and defensive roles across kinetic battlefields and digital domains, examines shifting geopolitical dynamics and ethical debates, evaluates security risks and vulnerabilities, and extrapolates emerging trends. AI-enabled targeting systems, autonomous drones, and cyber defense platforms saw practical use in disputes (Ukraine, Middle East), offering unprecedented speed and efficiency while introducing vulnerabilities including adversarial attacks, algorithmic bias, and eroded accountability. Major powers accelerated AI integration, driving a global arms race. Simultaneously, urgent ethical and legal questions arose about autonomous lethal decision-making. AI tools unveiled capabilities for strengthening defenses and enabling new offensive tactics like automated malware generation, enhancing the AI attacker-defender duel. Looking ahead, generative AI, multidomain hybrid warfare, and fully autonomous systems will transform warfare while policymakers grapple with ensuring meaningful human control and international law compliance.
ER  - 

